# Official Qwen block-scaled FP8 checkpoint. Sole surviving Qwen3.8-27B variant on gx10 as of
# 2026-09-02: the unsloth NVFP4 quant (qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4) and the bf16 original (qwen3.8-27b)
# were both removed the same day after this FP8 checkpoint validated as the better choice.
#
# Validated 2026-09-02, two stability-battery runs (cold + warm), both all_passed=true:
#   - Decode: ~22.9 tok/s cold-start, ~26.9-31.9 tok/s warm (no spec-decode; concurrency=4,
#     512in/128out benchmark). CUTLASS FP8 GEMM path (vLLM auto-disables DeepGEMM on Blackwell;
#     forcing it back on via VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM=1 + CUTE_DSL_ARCH=sm_121a is untested on GB10's
#     specific SM variant and has a known crash mode on the neighboring SM120 -- not attempted).
#   - MMLU (62 subtasks, 5-shot limit, n=310): 0.842-0.874 -- strong, expected range for this
#     model size.
#
# WHY FP8 over the removed NVFP4 sibling despite NVFP4 being faster (67.8-74.3 tok/s): MTP
# spec-decode (k=3), which the NVFP4 recipe required for that speed, was found to badly corrupt
# loglikelihood/logprob-based scoring on this model+vLLM 0.27.1 combo -- MMLU collapsed to ~0.45
# (barely above the 0.25 random floor) with spec-decode ON vs ~0.84 OFF, on the IDENTICAL eval
# config, reproduced across both KV-cache-dtype variants tested. Generated text itself likely
# stayed correct (stability battery only checks successful completions, not logprob accuracy),
# but anything trusting logprobs (confidence scoring, guided decoding, eval harnesses) would have
# been silently unreliable. This FP8 config runs with SPEC_ARG/COMPILE_ARG explicitly cleared
# (no MTP) specifically to avoid that bug -- do not re-enable spec-decode on this model family
# without first re-verifying logprob correctness, not just throughput.
#
# NOT yet tried: recipes.vllm.ai's FP8 numbers (TP4/GB300, 2x RTX 5090) don't apply to this
# single-GPU GB10 box, so there's no external apples-to-apples throughput reference. A forum
# poster's Docker recipe (VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM=1, CUTE_DSL_ARCH=sm_121a, --max-num-batched-tokens
# 8192, --max-num-seqs 4, --max-model-len 212992) targets GB10's exact SM arch but ships no
# performance numbers and DeepGEMM's SM120-class Blackwell support is known-fragile -- judged not
# worth the risk for now (2026-09-02).

# --- UI metadata ---
UI_LABEL="Qwen3.8-27B-FP8"
UI_DESC="Official Qwen block-scaled FP8 checkpoint. No spec-decode (MTP k=3 was found to corrupt logprob/loglikelihood scoring on this model family -- see header). ~30.9GB, native 256K context, CUTLASS FP8 GEMM path (DeepGEMM unavailable/untested on GB10's sm_121a). Validated 2026-09-02: full stability battery passed, MMLU ~84-87%, ~27-32 tok/s decode -- the accuracy-safe default for this model."
UI_SIZE="~30.9 GB · FP8 block-scaled · vision · 256K ctx"
UI_SPEED="~27-32 tok/s (measured 2026-09-02, no spec-decode)"
UI_USE_CASES="Vision Q&A, Long-context (256K) reading, Agentic tool-use"
EXPERIMENTAL="0"

# --- Serve recipe ---
SERVE_MODEL="Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8"
SERVED_NAME="qwen3.8-27b-fp8"
SERVE_CONTAINER="swap-vllm-qwen3.8-27b-fp8"
SERVE_PORT="8002"
MAX_LEN="262144"
GPU_UTIL="0.85"
QUANT="fp8"
TOOLS="1"
REASONING_PARSER="qwen3"
KV_ARG=""
GENCFG_ARG=""
EXTRA_ARGS=""
SPEC_ARG=""
COMPILE_ARG=""
